If 40% of notional income is awarded for future prospects, the amount awarded for loss of income works out to Rs.22,68,000/- [Rs.12,000/- X 40% = Rs.4,800/-; Rs.12,000/- +
Rs.4,800/- = Rs.16,800/-; Rs.16,800/- X 1/4 = Rs.4,200/-; Rs.16,800/- - Rs.4,200/- = Rs.12,600/-;
Rs.12,600/- X 12 X 15 = Rs.22,68,000/-].
